1
00:00:01,721 --> 00:00:03,931
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
IN A DUSTY UNIVERSE

3
00:01:38,859 --> 00:01:40,152
- [light switch clicks]
- Uh--

4
00:01:40,236 --> 00:01:42,571
Well, you've got some stuff in here.

5
00:01:42,655 --> 00:01:45,407
You made it sound like all you had
was four walls and a door.

6
00:01:45,491 --> 00:01:47,618
Yeah. The more you own,
the more it owns you.

7
00:01:47,701 --> 00:01:48,702
[Jack chuckles]

8
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,455
{\an8}High School Proficiency exam?

9
00:01:51,539 --> 00:01:53,207
{\an8}[Legoshi] Yeah. [inhales]

10
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:56,752
{\an8}If I want to work at the insect museum,
I need a high school diploma.

11
00:01:56,836 --> 00:01:59,296
Should've thought about that
before I dropped out.

12
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,173
[Jack] You're trying to get a job there?

13
00:02:01,257 --> 00:02:04,802
Oh, well... [chuckles]
...it's just a dream, for now.

14
00:02:04,885 --> 00:02:06,595
Okay, a dream.

15
00:02:06,679 --> 00:02:08,556
Yeah, I get it.

16
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,141
Gotta have those.

17
00:02:12,893 --> 00:02:15,896
Hey, full moon's on its way.

18
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:17,940
Sometimes when there's a full moon out,

19
00:02:18,023 --> 00:02:20,776
Kolo and I see
who has the best pretend howl.

20
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:22,653
[Legoshi]
Howling's banned on campus, right?

21
00:02:22,736 --> 00:02:24,989
Well, we just pretend.

22
00:02:25,072 --> 00:02:27,408
We're real quiet about it.

23
00:02:27,491 --> 00:02:31,328
Knowing your voice could reach out
into the night sure is a comfort.

24
00:02:33,414 --> 00:02:35,082
[Legoshi]
<i>His tail's not wagging.</i>

25
00:02:35,791 --> 00:02:38,210
[Jack] I bet you've got
a great howl, Legoshi.

26
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,881
- Hey, Jack?
- [Jack] Hmm?

27
00:02:42,798 --> 00:02:44,300
Is everything all right?

28
00:02:45,634 --> 00:02:48,345
You seem... a little off.

29
00:02:49,179 --> 00:02:50,973
Well, I...

30
00:02:51,056 --> 00:02:54,351
I guess it's just these advanced classes,
they're kinda wearing me out.

31
00:02:54,435 --> 00:02:57,396
These classes, are they that tough?

32
00:02:57,479 --> 00:02:59,690
Well, maybe?

33
00:03:00,608 --> 00:03:02,359
Not tough.

34
00:03:02,443 --> 00:03:05,362
Mm. More like a unique experience.

35
00:03:05,446 --> 00:03:06,780
Unique, how?

36
00:03:06,864 --> 00:03:09,199
One of the classes, everyone's dogs.

37
00:03:09,283 --> 00:03:10,117
Everyone?

38
00:03:10,701 --> 00:03:12,578
Makes sense if you think about it.

39
00:03:12,661 --> 00:03:15,122
I mean, with us dogs,
we were specifically bred

40
00:03:15,205 --> 00:03:16,749
to have advanced intelligence.

41
00:03:16,832 --> 00:03:20,002
So you're saying that dogs
are really good at studying?

42
00:03:20,085 --> 00:03:21,337
[Jack] Mmm.

43
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:24,798
{\an8}It also means we're cool under pressure.

44
00:03:24,882 --> 00:03:27,468
{\an8}We don't let our emotions
get the better of us.

45
00:03:27,551 --> 00:03:29,178
END OF THE FIRST CARNIVORE-HERBIVORE WAR

46
00:03:29,261 --> 00:03:31,096
<i>In the advanced courses,</i>

47
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,516
<i>they make us study things
that are not taught in regular classes.</i>

48
00:03:35,559 --> 00:03:38,812
<i>Like which species drove another species
to extinction...</i>

49
00:03:39,438 --> 00:03:41,357
<i>and which species preyed on which.</i>

50
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:44,068
[inhales] <i>And we sit there,</i>

51
00:03:44,151 --> 00:03:46,570
<i>just copying it all into our notebooks.</i>

52
00:03:46,654 --> 00:03:50,157
<i>Lapping up these facts,
like nothing even happened.</i>

53
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:53,285
<i>And when class is over,</i>

54
00:03:53,369 --> 00:03:55,663
<i>we smile and wave like it's no big deal.</i>

55
00:03:56,705 --> 00:03:59,541
<i>Like we're just robots
doing what we're programmed to do.</i>

56
00:04:01,627 --> 00:04:05,256
If you were in this class,
I don't think you'd have a very good time.

57
00:04:06,006 --> 00:04:08,092
Doesn't seem you're having
a good time, though.

58
00:04:08,175 --> 00:04:11,804
If that's the case,
why don't I drop the class?

59
00:04:11,887 --> 00:04:13,722
Why don't I feel disgusted?

60
00:04:13,806 --> 00:04:15,557
Is it because I'm a dog?

61
00:04:15,641 --> 00:04:17,351
Born to be calm and rational?

62
00:04:18,227 --> 00:04:19,603
Guess that's my nature.

63
00:04:22,189 --> 00:04:24,441
I've got this pit in my stomach.

64
00:04:25,359 --> 00:04:28,445
Like, what if I'm actually
just numb on the inside?

65
00:04:29,738 --> 00:04:32,408
If I could at least cry,
that would be something.

66
00:04:32,491 --> 00:04:33,784
At least I could feel.

67
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:36,287
So that's why you were carrying this?

68
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:37,288
Uh...

69
00:04:38,664 --> 00:04:39,748
Yeah.

70
00:04:39,832 --> 00:04:40,916
Uh...

71
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,543
I use onions.

72
00:04:42,626 --> 00:04:45,296
This is one way I can force myself to cry.

73
00:04:45,379 --> 00:04:46,255
Huh?

74
00:04:47,172 --> 00:04:48,841
- Let me show you what I mean.
- Um...

75
00:04:49,675 --> 00:04:51,051
This is my salvation.

76
00:04:51,135 --> 00:04:52,469
Hold on a sec!

77
00:04:53,554 --> 00:04:55,139
- [Jack grunts]
- Whoa, Jack, hey!

78
00:04:55,222 --> 00:04:58,142
[crying] I can't stand myself.
Being a Labrador!

79
00:04:58,225 --> 00:05:02,479
If all dogs are like this,
we'll end up dictators! [grunts]

80
00:05:02,563 --> 00:05:05,024
I'm not sure about that.
I, uh, I wouldn't...

81
00:05:05,107 --> 00:05:07,651
[crying] We're made to be obedient.

82
00:05:07,735 --> 00:05:09,528
If we were told to go on a killing spree,

83
00:05:09,611 --> 00:05:11,071
then that's what we'd do!

84
00:05:11,155 --> 00:05:12,531
Dogs are terrifying.

85
00:05:12,614 --> 00:05:14,450
And I'm a dog!

86
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:17,453
[gasps] Jack, come on!
You're more than just your species.

87
00:05:17,536 --> 00:05:19,788
You feel the way you do
because you're Jack.

88
00:05:19,872 --> 00:05:21,749
Before anything, you're Jack!

89
00:05:21,832 --> 00:05:22,958
[crying]

90
00:05:23,042 --> 00:05:25,544
How do you know what I am?

91
00:05:25,627 --> 00:05:28,130
How can you really know what's inside?

92
00:05:28,213 --> 00:05:30,299
[soft music playing]

93
00:05:30,382 --> 00:05:32,384
Because we grew up together.

94
00:05:32,926 --> 00:05:35,387
[sobbing softly]

95
00:05:35,471 --> 00:05:36,680
Does that make sense?

96
00:05:38,474 --> 00:05:40,225
[Jack]
<i>Together?</i>

97
00:05:40,309 --> 00:05:41,602
<i>I don't know.</i>

98
00:05:42,936 --> 00:05:45,773
<i>You left me behind
and grew up on your own.</i>

99
00:05:46,732 --> 00:05:48,150
<i>Free to do what you wanted.</i>

100
00:05:48,233 --> 00:05:50,652
<i>I can't relate to that.</i>

101
00:05:51,445 --> 00:05:52,863
Come on.

102
00:05:52,946 --> 00:05:54,531
Let's cheer you up.

103
00:05:55,532 --> 00:05:58,077
How about we get
that tail wagging again, Jack?

104
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,203
[Jack sniffles]

105
00:05:59,995 --> 00:06:00,829
[munching]

106
00:06:00,913 --> 00:06:03,665
[gasps] You idiot! Are you crazy?

107
00:06:03,749 --> 00:06:05,125
You can't eat an onion!

108
00:06:05,209 --> 00:06:07,586
You think I'll be obedient
just because I'm a dog?

109
00:06:07,669 --> 00:06:09,630
What are you saying, do you wanna die?

110
00:06:09,713 --> 00:06:12,299
Even Labradors need to rebel sometimes!

111
00:06:12,841 --> 00:06:14,510
[choking]

112
00:06:14,593 --> 00:06:16,345
Throw it up! Hear me?

113
00:06:16,428 --> 00:06:18,472
[gagging]

114
00:06:19,056 --> 00:06:20,224
Spit it all out!

115
00:06:20,307 --> 00:06:22,726
[Jack gagging]

116
00:06:23,393 --> 00:06:27,981
[Jack] <i>I can feel Legoshi's sharp claws
hitting the back of my throat.</i>

117
00:06:28,065 --> 00:06:29,274
<i>It hurts a lot.</i>

118
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,902
<i>This is who he is.</i>

119
00:06:31,985 --> 00:06:33,237
<i>Nothing's changed.</i>

120
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,447
<i>He's always been this way.</i>

121
00:06:35,531 --> 00:06:37,699
[gagging]

122
00:06:39,451 --> 00:06:42,204
[Jack breathing heavily]

123
00:06:42,287 --> 00:06:43,539
[Legoshi]
Sorry, bud.

124
00:06:43,622 --> 00:06:45,874
Onions kill canines.

125
00:06:45,958 --> 00:06:47,292
That would have been it.

126
00:06:49,211 --> 00:06:51,130
I need you to take care of yourself.

127
00:06:52,339 --> 00:06:55,467
Because my hope is,
one day when we're old,

128
00:06:55,551 --> 00:06:59,054
you and I will still be
laughing and crying together.

129
00:06:59,138 --> 00:07:00,848
Just like we did today.

130
00:07:01,807 --> 00:07:05,352
That's quite the dream, you mangy wolf.

131
00:07:06,311 --> 00:07:08,730
Because you're a real pain in the tail.

132
00:07:16,738 --> 00:07:20,033
[howling in distance]

133
00:07:20,117 --> 00:07:20,993
[Jack]
Hmm?

134
00:07:22,369 --> 00:07:24,413
[howling continues]

135
00:07:24,496 --> 00:07:26,039
[chuckles]

136
00:07:27,458 --> 00:07:30,961
[howls]

137
00:07:31,044 --> 00:07:32,713
Legoshi! [chuckles]

138
00:07:33,547 --> 00:07:36,758
[Legoshi howling]

139
00:07:36,842 --> 00:07:39,178
[woman vocalizing]

140
00:07:45,809 --> 00:07:47,436
Melda?

141
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:49,855
I'm sorry, but I'm at a loss.

142
00:07:49,938 --> 00:07:53,609
The drug that was unveiled
at the masquerade party,

143
00:07:53,692 --> 00:07:57,029
we know the Shishigumi
transported it from here.

144
00:07:57,112 --> 00:07:58,906
You don't say!

145
00:07:58,989 --> 00:08:00,866
What kind of drug is this?

146
00:08:00,949 --> 00:08:02,451
That's what I'm asking you.

147
00:08:04,578 --> 00:08:05,662
Is that what this is?

148
00:08:05,746 --> 00:08:07,956
- Oh, what an imagination.
- [sniffs]

149
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:10,125
That's my top-notch Kopi Luwak.

150
00:08:13,253 --> 00:08:15,464
You know there are some types of foods,

151
00:08:15,547 --> 00:08:18,383
those produced by animals,
like eggs or milk,

152
00:08:18,467 --> 00:08:22,513
that can be satisfying in a way
that's similar to meat,

153
00:08:22,596 --> 00:08:24,932
just like this Kopi Luwak.

154
00:08:25,015 --> 00:08:28,894
[Yahya grunting]

155
00:08:31,271 --> 00:08:33,607
[exhales, sniffles]

156
00:08:33,690 --> 00:08:37,277
[Deshico] <i>Hmm.
Why would it affect an herbivore?</i>

157
00:08:37,861 --> 00:08:39,905
Your first time trying Kopi Luwak?

158
00:08:39,988 --> 00:08:41,114
Yeah.

159
00:08:41,198 --> 00:08:44,243
You know, it's carnivores
that usually react that way.

160
00:08:44,826 --> 00:08:48,580
[Yahya] <i>Is it because my carrots
absorbed meat nutrients?</i>

161
00:08:49,456 --> 00:08:53,001
Could it be possible that... you're mixed?

162
00:08:53,085 --> 00:08:55,003
What makes you say that?

163
00:08:55,087 --> 00:08:57,297
It makes some sense.

164
00:08:57,381 --> 00:09:00,092
First of all,
there's your exceptional decisiveness.

165
00:09:00,175 --> 00:09:03,679
And when approaching a situation,
you're passionately all-in.

166
00:09:03,762 --> 00:09:06,306
And you don't hesitate to use violence.

167
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:07,891
You abhor criticism,

168
00:09:07,975 --> 00:09:10,269
and your self-confidence
borders on arrogance.

169
00:09:10,352 --> 00:09:11,353
[Yahya chuckles]

170
00:09:11,436 --> 00:09:16,191
Of course, these traits don't necessarily
confirm your hybrid nature.

171
00:09:16,275 --> 00:09:20,404
However, you do remind me
of a hybrid specimen I studied.

172
00:09:20,487 --> 00:09:21,780
You mean Melon?

173
00:09:21,863 --> 00:09:23,282
Can't say.

174
00:09:23,365 --> 00:09:27,369
As a research institute,
we have strict rules of confidentiality.

175
00:09:27,452 --> 00:09:29,204
How convenient.

176
00:09:29,288 --> 00:09:32,874
Did you write down a mixed species'
weakness in your research notes?

177
00:09:32,958 --> 00:09:34,334
[chuckles]

178
00:09:34,418 --> 00:09:36,128
You're quite the blunt instrument.

179
00:09:36,211 --> 00:09:38,422
- I'm not one for small talk.
- I've noticed.

180
00:09:39,298 --> 00:09:42,426
Well, the academic consensus seems to be...

181
00:09:42,509 --> 00:09:46,054
that mixed species
quite often lack a strong appetite.

182
00:09:46,138 --> 00:09:49,391
And they display
a weaker than normal sex drive.

183
00:09:49,474 --> 00:09:52,561
Those sound like an advantage
in this day and age.

184
00:09:52,644 --> 00:09:55,772
Possibly, but I imagine
it's still difficult.

185
00:09:55,856 --> 00:09:58,775
Never feeling satisfied
no matter what they eat?

186
00:09:59,985 --> 00:10:03,822
[Yahya] <i>"Never feeling satisfied
no matter what they eat"?</i>

187
00:10:05,032 --> 00:10:07,284
- [panting]
- [boy 1] You're not a real herbivore!

188
00:10:07,367 --> 00:10:09,369
- Look at him run!
- [boy 2] Nowhere to hide!

189
00:10:09,453 --> 00:10:10,662
[boy 1] Do it! Jump!

190
00:10:10,746 --> 00:10:13,373
There's no reality
where you could become a professor.

191
00:10:13,457 --> 00:10:15,584
You're not a real herbivore,
you half-breed.

192
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:18,211
[all mocking]

193
00:10:18,295 --> 00:10:20,672
Being part feline,
I'm sure you'll land on your feet.

194
00:10:21,298 --> 00:10:22,507
[screams]

195
00:10:24,134 --> 00:10:25,302
[thuds]

196
00:10:29,514 --> 00:10:32,100
Let's find a bag to put this evidence in.

197
00:10:33,268 --> 00:10:35,062
- Uh, yeah.
- [thunder rumbles]

198
00:10:37,147 --> 00:10:38,398
Hmm.

199
00:10:41,652 --> 00:10:43,362
Close the windows, if you don't mind.

200
00:10:44,738 --> 00:10:46,865
COEXISTENCE THEORY

201
00:10:46,948 --> 00:10:49,034
[straining]

202
00:10:49,618 --> 00:10:51,536
- So, Haru...
- Yes?

203
00:10:52,329 --> 00:10:53,664
You were telling me,

204
00:10:53,747 --> 00:10:56,375
you've been in a situation
where your life was in danger.

205
00:10:57,417 --> 00:11:00,587
Well, being a rabbit,
it's not that unusual.

206
00:11:00,671 --> 00:11:03,548
Are you afraid of being around carnivores?

207
00:11:03,632 --> 00:11:06,051
Um... If you're afraid all the time,

208
00:11:06,134 --> 00:11:08,762
it makes it hard to get
to know other species, right?

209
00:11:08,845 --> 00:11:10,430
That'd be scary too.

210
00:11:10,514 --> 00:11:11,765
As scary as being eaten?

211
00:11:11,848 --> 00:11:13,725
Yeah, I think so. Whoa!

212
00:11:13,809 --> 00:11:15,769
[grunts] Oh.

213
00:11:15,852 --> 00:11:19,231
I'm all right, it's... [groans]

214
00:11:19,731 --> 00:11:22,150
If you stick with that mindset
your whole life,

215
00:11:22,234 --> 00:11:25,153
- someday you may actually get eaten.
- [groaning]

216
00:11:25,237 --> 00:11:27,697
If I have to live in the company of death,

217
00:11:27,781 --> 00:11:29,658
I prefer to focus on love.

218
00:11:30,867 --> 00:11:32,369
[thunder rumbling]

219
00:11:32,452 --> 00:11:35,831
Wow, it's really coming down!

220
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:40,794
[Melon] <i>Inside that fragile little body
clinging to every heartbeat...</i>

221
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:46,383
<i>there's a universe of thoughts
and ideas stirring within her.</i>

222
00:11:46,466 --> 00:11:47,551
[laughs]

223
00:11:47,634 --> 00:11:49,010
This rain is crazy!

224
00:11:49,845 --> 00:11:52,389
[Melon] <i>I do wonder...</i>

225
00:11:52,472 --> 00:11:55,851
<i>Could I taste those thoughts and emotions?</i>

226
00:11:56,893 --> 00:11:59,479
<i>Are they in her blood and flesh?</i>

227
00:11:59,563 --> 00:12:01,189
[salivates]

228
00:12:02,607 --> 00:12:03,692
<i>I think...</i>

229
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:07,821
<i>I wanna find out.</i>

230
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:10,365
[gasps]

231
00:12:13,326 --> 00:12:15,662
[Haru]
<i>I know this fear. I've felt it.</i>

232
00:12:16,413 --> 00:12:17,747
[exclaims]

233
00:12:17,831 --> 00:12:19,166
Just stop it!

234
00:12:19,249 --> 00:12:20,917
What's your species, Professor?

235
00:12:21,001 --> 00:12:22,127
[Melon]
Huh?

236
00:12:22,210 --> 00:12:26,548
Uh, well, the way you were holding me
wasn't romantic.

237
00:12:26,631 --> 00:12:29,593
It was almost like
how a carnivore catches an herbivore

238
00:12:29,676 --> 00:12:31,511
right before they, uh...

239
00:12:31,595 --> 00:12:34,931
But, I... I always need to be careful
because I'm a rabbit,

240
00:12:35,015 --> 00:12:37,559
but it doesn't help
that I've had a few close calls.

241
00:12:37,642 --> 00:12:39,644
Uh, it's just... I'm just rambling.

242
00:12:39,728 --> 00:12:41,730
{\an8}- [Haru chuckles nervously]
- [Melon] Not to worry.

243
00:12:41,813 --> 00:12:43,815
{\an8}As you can see, I'm a gazelle.

244
00:12:44,441 --> 00:12:47,068
Oh, uh, yes, of course you are. [chuckles]

245
00:12:47,152 --> 00:12:48,653
A gazelle, yes.

246
00:12:48,737 --> 00:12:51,072
Uh, no way you're a carnivore, but, um...

247
00:12:52,365 --> 00:12:54,284
Uh, Professor...

248
00:12:54,367 --> 00:12:58,038
When you grabbed me,
was that you trying to make a move?

249
00:12:58,121 --> 00:13:00,207
- [thunder rumbles]
- [chuckles nervously]

250
00:13:00,290 --> 00:13:05,003
I'm flattered, but, uh, there's a boy
I kind of like right now and, um...

251
00:13:05,086 --> 00:13:07,255
I was kind of a late bloomer
with dating,

252
00:13:07,339 --> 00:13:09,883
so I'm not really used
to how it all works.

253
00:13:09,966 --> 00:13:11,551
- [gasps]
- [clicking]

254
00:13:16,598 --> 00:13:18,225
- [thunder crashes]
- [Melon groans]

255
00:13:19,184 --> 00:13:21,228
[Melon laughing]

256
00:13:23,355 --> 00:13:24,397
[groans]

257
00:13:26,066 --> 00:13:28,068
I knew it. [inhales]

258
00:13:28,735 --> 00:13:31,947
First time something like this
has happened. [inhales sharply]

259
00:13:32,697 --> 00:13:36,034
The pain isn't that bad... right now.

260
00:13:36,117 --> 00:13:37,536
[inhales sharply]

261
00:13:37,619 --> 00:13:39,871
The pain in my heart might be worse.

262
00:13:39,955 --> 00:13:41,915
- [Melon inhales]
- [Haru shudders]

263
00:13:41,998 --> 00:13:45,335
[Melon] This has certainly
gotten complicated. [chuckles]

264
00:13:45,418 --> 00:13:46,753
Hasn't it?

265
00:13:47,754 --> 00:13:49,965
[thunder crashes]

266
00:14:02,602 --> 00:14:04,312
[Legoshi]
Appreciate your business.

267
00:14:04,396 --> 00:14:06,189
Hey, uh, before you go.

268
00:14:06,273 --> 00:14:07,899
You guys have a secret menu, right?

269
00:14:07,983 --> 00:14:09,818
What? I don't know anything about that.

270
00:14:09,901 --> 00:14:12,028
Come on, you don't have to play dumb.

271
00:14:12,112 --> 00:14:14,573
I want something exotic.
Udon with meat.

272
00:14:14,656 --> 00:14:16,032
We don't have anything like that.

273
00:14:16,116 --> 00:14:18,410
The fact that you're acting like this
tells me you do.

274
00:14:18,493 --> 00:14:20,078
Ugh. Gotta go.

275
00:14:21,162 --> 00:14:22,706
[male bear]
He said no.

276
00:14:22,789 --> 00:14:25,166
I'll buy some lamb
at the black market tomorrow.

277
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:28,503
[female bear] Let's do that.
Ooh, we can find a good meat udon recipe!

278
00:14:28,587 --> 00:14:31,590
[Legoshi] <i>Am I being extreme?</i>

279
00:14:31,673 --> 00:14:33,884
<i>It does seem to make 'em happy.</i>

280
00:14:33,967 --> 00:14:35,969
[Yahya]
I've seen that troubled face before.

281
00:14:36,052 --> 00:14:36,970
Hm? Oh.

282
00:14:37,053 --> 00:14:39,139
Mr. Yahya! Hey.

283
00:14:39,222 --> 00:14:41,308
You're walking on that leg just fine.

284
00:14:41,391 --> 00:14:43,059
So, did you find Melon?

285
00:14:43,143 --> 00:14:45,270
[Legoshi]
Uh, well, uh...

286
00:14:45,353 --> 00:14:49,149
For starters, how about giving back
that mask you borrowed?

287
00:14:49,733 --> 00:14:52,193
Uh... Sorry, sir.

288
00:14:52,277 --> 00:14:55,113
I ended up dropping it into the sea.

289
00:14:55,196 --> 00:14:57,198
Or, actually, I was dropped.

290
00:14:57,282 --> 00:14:59,200
So you did meet Melon?

291
00:14:59,284 --> 00:15:00,577
Very brave.

292
00:15:02,162 --> 00:15:05,665
You said you were done
with the Melon situation.

293
00:15:05,749 --> 00:15:07,292
Did something else come up?

294
00:15:07,375 --> 00:15:10,629
Tell me more about this conversation
you had with Melon.

295
00:15:11,379 --> 00:15:12,923
It was pretty terrible.

296
00:15:13,548 --> 00:15:14,633
I was too naive.

297
00:15:14,716 --> 00:15:15,800
Figured as much.

298
00:15:17,177 --> 00:15:19,721
True evil is real, and it's him.

299
00:15:19,804 --> 00:15:21,431
It was terrifying.

300
00:15:22,474 --> 00:15:24,517
Man, I was so scared.

301
00:15:24,601 --> 00:15:25,977
Guess I still am.

302
00:15:26,061 --> 00:15:29,439
So even the invincible Legoshi
gets scared?

303
00:15:29,522 --> 00:15:32,734
[groans softly]
He enjoyed watching me die.

304
00:15:33,276 --> 00:15:36,196
In my head, I pictured flames.

305
00:15:36,738 --> 00:15:39,115
This huge fire inside.

306
00:15:39,783 --> 00:15:42,202
And I know those flames.

307
00:15:42,285 --> 00:15:46,581
Whenever I ate meat,
when I ended up in a fight...

308
00:15:48,416 --> 00:15:50,543
I saw those flames inside.

309
00:15:51,419 --> 00:15:53,964
What if I've got a Melon inside me?

310
00:15:54,047 --> 00:15:56,424
That's what... That's what I'm afraid of.

311
00:15:57,384 --> 00:15:59,970
[Yahya] <i>So this is what makes
Melon so terrifying.</i>

312
00:16:00,845 --> 00:16:02,097
I don't want to face him.

313
00:16:03,807 --> 00:16:04,975
I see.

314
00:16:05,892 --> 00:16:07,978
I'm sorry about losing the mask,

315
00:16:08,061 --> 00:16:09,688
but I need to go.

316
00:16:10,563 --> 00:16:12,399
They'll dock my pay if I take too long.

317
00:16:12,482 --> 00:16:14,859
Yeah. Do what you gotta do.

318
00:16:25,704 --> 00:16:30,625
[Legoshi] <i>Will I always fear that beast
that lives inside me?</i>

319
00:16:31,376 --> 00:16:35,839
[faint humming]

320
00:16:35,922 --> 00:16:37,340
Huh?

321
00:16:38,508 --> 00:16:40,427
[panting]

322
00:16:45,015 --> 00:16:46,224
[chuckles]

323
00:16:46,307 --> 00:16:49,561
I was getting pretty tired of waiting
for the lone wolf to return.

324
00:16:49,644 --> 00:16:52,897
[chuckles]

325
00:16:53,857 --> 00:16:55,692
[Haru]
All right, coming in.

326
00:16:56,776 --> 00:16:59,863
- Hey, look how cozy this is.
- Mmm.

327
00:17:00,739 --> 00:17:04,117
Oh, the mint plant is really healthy,
look at you!

328
00:17:05,702 --> 00:17:09,080
[Legoshi] <i>Interesting.
I've got a great sense of smell.</i>

329
00:17:09,998 --> 00:17:12,584
<i>Another male. I can smell him on her!</i>

330
00:17:13,293 --> 00:17:15,170
<i>Who the hell was he?</i>

331
00:17:15,253 --> 00:17:17,255
[Haru]
I'll bring you some fertilizer.

332
00:17:17,338 --> 00:17:20,216
[Legoshi] <i>Ugh!
The rain's messing up the scent!</i>

333
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,509
Hey, Legoshi?

334
00:17:21,593 --> 00:17:22,594
Huh?

335
00:17:22,677 --> 00:17:25,263
Trains are done for the night.
Can I just stay here?

336
00:17:25,346 --> 00:17:26,973
Oh. Stay?

337
00:17:27,057 --> 00:17:28,099
Overnight?

338
00:17:28,183 --> 00:17:29,267
What?

339
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:32,687
[chuckles] Don't worry.
I even brought my own toothbrush.

340
00:17:32,771 --> 00:17:33,855
- Uh...
- See?

341
00:17:34,939 --> 00:17:37,317
Oh. [chuckling]

342
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,110
[Haru sipping]

343
00:17:39,194 --> 00:17:40,945
Mm. This tea is so yummy!

344
00:17:41,029 --> 00:17:43,031
[Legoshi] Mmm.

345
00:17:43,114 --> 00:17:44,699
- Haru, uh...
- Hm?

346
00:17:44,783 --> 00:17:46,201
Well, um...

347
00:17:46,785 --> 00:17:47,911
[laughs nervously]

348
00:17:47,994 --> 00:17:50,205
Have... Have you been enjoying yourself?

349
00:17:50,288 --> 00:17:51,831
Uh, on campus, I mean.

350
00:17:51,915 --> 00:17:53,917
Is there something you wanna talk about?

351
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,461
No! Uh, I was just making conversation.

352
00:17:56,544 --> 00:17:58,213
And is that why your tail's all raised?

353
00:17:58,296 --> 00:18:00,965
Oh. [chuckles] Come on.
I was just thinking...

354
00:18:01,049 --> 00:18:04,969
that schools have a lot
of guys and girls interacting and...

355
00:18:05,053 --> 00:18:06,137
[Haru] Legoshi!

356
00:18:06,221 --> 00:18:07,972
What do you think this is?

357
00:18:08,056 --> 00:18:11,184
You think you can lock a girl down
without even dangling a carrot?

358
00:18:11,267 --> 00:18:13,978
Exactly how long am I supposed
to wait for even a kiss?

359
00:18:14,062 --> 00:18:15,814
Hey now, slow down!

360
00:18:15,897 --> 00:18:17,273
What about the risks?

361
00:18:17,357 --> 00:18:20,443
Physically, socially, and economically...

362
00:18:20,527 --> 00:18:22,987
[sighs] You're not as smart
as you think you are.

363
00:18:23,071 --> 00:18:24,531
Hey, now.

364
00:18:24,614 --> 00:18:27,575
And, about that, with the physical stuff...

365
00:18:28,201 --> 00:18:29,619
We don't know, do we?

366
00:18:29,702 --> 00:18:30,703
Huh?

367
00:18:30,787 --> 00:18:32,914
We have no idea how it would work,

368
00:18:32,997 --> 00:18:35,166
{\an8}because you literally
haven't done anything yet.

369
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:36,126
{\an8}Huh?

370
00:18:36,209 --> 00:18:38,711
{\an8}How will we ever know
if you don't show me?

371
00:18:38,795 --> 00:18:40,296
{\an8}[Legoshi]
<i>Oh, this is intense.</i>

372
00:18:40,797 --> 00:18:41,756
{\an8}Are you serious?

373
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,050
- Don't I look serious?
- Uh...

374
00:18:44,134 --> 00:18:46,469
Show me, Legoshi. Give it to me!

375
00:18:46,553 --> 00:18:48,930
- You can eat me any time.
- Uh...

376
00:18:49,013 --> 00:18:51,474
And there's not a damn thing
I can do about it!

377
00:18:51,558 --> 00:18:54,227
So, for tonight,
just let me have a taste of you.

378
00:18:58,231 --> 00:18:59,649
[groaning]

379
00:18:59,732 --> 00:19:01,276
[unzipping]

380
00:19:03,528 --> 00:19:07,740
[Legoshi] <i>Haru,
since the day I fell in love with you,</i>

381
00:19:07,824 --> 00:19:10,201
<i>something's always been
in the back of my mind.</i>

382
00:19:12,745 --> 00:19:16,416
<i>How, if I were a female rabbit
and you were a male wolf...</i>

383
00:19:17,417 --> 00:19:21,045
<i>How, if you held me
or if you ate me...</i>

384
00:19:21,838 --> 00:19:24,465
<i>I'd be happy. Either way.</i>

385
00:19:24,549 --> 00:19:25,758
[Haru sighs]

386
00:19:26,509 --> 00:19:28,303
I'm really sorry.

387
00:19:28,386 --> 00:19:30,305
I'm not normally like this.

388
00:19:30,388 --> 00:19:31,514
What?

389
00:19:31,598 --> 00:19:34,225
Why would you think you have to apologize?

390
00:19:35,685 --> 00:19:38,021
I'm really happy you opened up to me.

391
00:19:38,605 --> 00:19:40,231
I wasn't sure you had it in you.

392
00:19:44,277 --> 00:19:46,988
[Legoshi]
<i>Sitting here in this sparse room,</i>

393
00:19:48,072 --> 00:19:53,328
<i>her fur and mine
float in the air, sparkling,</i>

394
00:19:53,411 --> 00:19:57,081
<i>making everything feel... strangely unreal.</i>

395
00:19:57,790 --> 00:20:00,752
<i>Forget the drama
of mixed species marriage.</i>

396
00:20:00,835 --> 00:20:03,046
<i>Forget society's opinions.</i>

397
00:20:03,129 --> 00:20:05,340
<i>If this room could be our own universe,</i>

398
00:20:05,423 --> 00:20:08,426
<i>and all that existed
was just the two of us,</i>

399
00:20:08,509 --> 00:20:10,678
<i>then here, I could--</i>

400
00:20:10,762 --> 00:20:12,055
Hey, how'd you get that?

401
00:20:12,138 --> 00:20:14,140
Hm? What? Oh.

402
00:20:14,224 --> 00:20:16,809
- And how'd that happen?
- [laughs] I fell down.

403
00:20:16,893 --> 00:20:19,354
Like I haven't heard that lie
from a guy before.

404
00:20:19,437 --> 00:20:21,356
And that's not the only injury you have.

405
00:20:21,439 --> 00:20:22,690
Oh. [chuckles]

406
00:20:22,774 --> 00:20:24,859
Oh, Legoshi, my word.

407
00:20:24,943 --> 00:20:28,488
I guess, when all is said and done,
you're a true carnivore.

408
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:29,864
You're a wolf.

409
00:20:29,948 --> 00:20:31,282
You're born with that instinct.

410
00:20:31,366 --> 00:20:33,952
I mean, violence and danger
is part of who you are.

411
00:20:34,035 --> 00:20:36,788
- Mm.
- It is what it is.

412
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:40,291
However, I'm gonna bet
you're more mature than that!

413
00:20:40,375 --> 00:20:41,960
[Legoshi grunts]

414
00:20:45,546 --> 00:20:47,257
Hey, how about from now on,

415
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:50,051
I help you live your life
more like an adult.

416
00:20:50,134 --> 00:20:51,803
Not all at once.

417
00:20:52,387 --> 00:20:55,556
Little by little. Yeah?

418
00:20:57,684 --> 00:20:59,060
I think I'd like that.

419
00:20:59,978 --> 00:21:01,437
All right then.

420
00:21:02,397 --> 00:21:04,983
The parts of us we haven't shared,

421
00:21:05,066 --> 00:21:07,485
we'll show them to each other
a bit at a time.

422
00:21:07,568 --> 00:21:10,738
[Legoshi chuckles] I'm pretty sure
you saw more than a bit tonight.

423
00:21:10,822 --> 00:21:12,907
[Haru laughs] You think so?

424
00:21:13,866 --> 00:21:16,327
{\an8}[softly] Thump, thump, thump...

425
00:21:18,079 --> 00:21:19,831
{\an8}It's the sound of you living.

426
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:24,043
{\an8}Is that also a part you don't know?

427
00:21:25,003 --> 00:21:26,796
{\an8}Mm-mm.

428
00:21:26,879 --> 00:21:28,756
{\an8}It's the part I know best.

429
00:21:39,267 --> 00:21:41,644
[groans softly]

430
00:21:41,728 --> 00:21:43,438
[smacks lips]

431
00:21:44,647 --> 00:21:46,232
Mmm.

432
00:21:51,404 --> 00:21:52,322
Haru?

433
00:21:53,406 --> 00:21:54,449
[groans]

434
00:21:56,909 --> 00:22:00,913
[dramatic music playing]

435
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:03,583
[closing song playing]
